{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>South of Kadesh Barnea.</b> It is puzzling to the master Bekhor Shor, for here it implies that Kadesh Barnea was part of the land of Canaan, but Moses our teacher did not cross the Jordan, and from Kadesh Barnea he sent the spies, as it is written: ״בשלוח אותם מקדש ברנע״. And it seems to me that there were two Kadesh Barneas, as is stated in chapter 3 of Makkot: Rabbi Yosi said, there were two Kadesh. And likewise in Joshua it is counted among the towns across the Jordan. And likewise Rashi explained that there were two Mount HaHar, because we find that Aaron died at Mount HaHar, which was not across the Jordan, and here it implies that it is in the land of Canaan, as it is written: ״תתאו לכם הר ההר״."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:30.623989850Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}